      "start_seconds": 0.84,
      "end_seconds": 6.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "hi there, the chair's free, sit down start wherever you like, I'm listening"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.25,
      "end_seconds": 16.91,
      "duration_seconds": 9.66,
      "text": "Mainly I've been feeling slightly dizzy. That's why I came. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.67,
      "end_seconds": 21.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.34,
      "end_seconds": 33.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.05,
      "end_seconds": 61.04,
      "duration_seconds": 13.99,
      "text": "Okay: temp 36.5 degrees, pulse is 68 beats a minute, pressure 111 over 79. And SpO2 97 percent on room air. Alright, how many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.84,
      "end_seconds": 68.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.73,
      "text": "around about three months... no wait, it's more like two months"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.9,
      "end_seconds": 73.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.79,
      "end_seconds": 88.11,
      "duration_seconds": 10.32,
      "text": "actually, pretty severe, if I'm being honest. I've had a vague low ache too, for about two weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.75,
      "end_seconds": 103.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "Have you had any collapse, heavy bleeding, severe pain or shoulder tip pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.05,
      "end_seconds": 109.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "No, uh, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.8,
      "end_seconds": 113.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.32,
      "end_seconds": 116.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "no, nothing there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.46,
      "end_seconds": 123.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "what about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.59,
      "end_seconds": 126.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.46,
      "end_seconds": 128.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "And your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.32,
      "end_seconds": 133.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.88,
      "end_seconds": 136.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "So, do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.37,
      "end_seconds": 142.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.43,
      "end_seconds": 145.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.86,
      "end_seconds": 150.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.35,
      "end_seconds": 153.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.06,
      "end_seconds": 158.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.83,
      "end_seconds": 162.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Are you on any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.95,
      "end_seconds": 167.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "no, nothing at the moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.3,
      "end_seconds": 188.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Right, any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.44,
      "end_seconds": 200.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Yes, asthma. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.51,
      "end_seconds": 210.54,
      "duration_seconds": 9.03,
      "text": "Alright, asthma, that matches what I have here. Alright, are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.08,
      "end_seconds": 213.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "I've never had an allergy"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.13,
      "end_seconds": 219.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.89,
      "end_seconds": 228.59,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.61,
      "end_seconds": 230.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.33,
      "end_seconds": 250.35,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft with mild tenderness low on the left and the pregnancy test is positive."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.23,
      "end_seconds": 274.95,
      "duration_seconds": 20.72,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Let me tell you where I've got to. I think we're dealing with a pregnancy of unknown location, ectopic not excluded at this stage. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.18,
      "end_seconds": 278.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.12,
      "end_seconds": 300.56,
      "duration_seconds": 20.44,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like a pregnancy of unknown location, ectopic not excluded, but I'd like to confirm. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've been feeling slightly dizzy for two months, severe, and no severe pain or heavy bleeding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.67,
      "end_seconds": 303.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Mm, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.92,
      "end_seconds": 320.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "I think a hormone blood test makes sense here, for pregnancy of unknown location"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 321.3,
      "end_seconds": 323.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "The earliest is Friday, 10 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.98,
      "end_seconds": 325.97,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "That's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.22,
      "end_seconds": 351.7,
      "duration_seconds": 24.48,
      "text": "even with little pain this needs a scan within a day, and go to hospital if the pain gets worse i'd like you to see the early pregnancy unit as well, and I'll write the referral do get help quickly if you get severe pain or feel faint we'll catch up tomorrow does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.0,
      "end_seconds": 356.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "great, thank you for your help"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.74,
      "end_seconds": 359.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "so, see you soon"
